#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161798 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "2d698f44-e551-58a2-883b-3a992119bd76" :question/math-academy-id "e-9126" :question/problem "The joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a$.\n\n|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac a2$ | $a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $a$ | $\\dfrac 52a$ |" :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is\n\n$$\nS_X = \\{0,1\\}\n$$\n\nthe support of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nS_Y = \\{0,1\\}\n$$\n\nand therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS= S_X\\times S_Y = \\left\\{(0,0), (0,1), (1,0), (1,1) \\right\\}\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$, we must have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum\\limits_{(x,y) \\in S} f(x,y) = 1\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(0, 0) + f(0, 1) + f(1, 0) + f(1, 1) &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{a}{2} + a + a + \\frac{5}{2}a &= 1 \\\\\n5a &= 1 \\\\\na &= \\frac{1}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161808 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "f2789f6c-11d5-5132-91b3-be65dac4ce24" :question/math-academy-id "e-9203" :question/problem "Compute $P\\Big((X,Y) \\in \\{(2,3), (6,1) \\}\\Big)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.\n\n|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |" :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP((X, Y) ∈ {(2, 3), (6, 1)}) &= P((X, Y) = (2, 3)) + P((X, Y) = (6, 1)) \\\\\n&= f(2, 3) + f(6, 1) \\\\\n&= 0.25 + 0.3 \\\\\n&= 0.55\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161809 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "01b86f31-f31e-567d-b798-fc0f10a4d0b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-9204" :question/problem "Compute $P\\left(X\\cdot Y \\geq 4 \\right)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.\n\n|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |" :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(X \\cdot Y \\ge 4) &= P((X, Y) ∈ {(1, 4), (2, 2), (2, 4)}) \\\\\n&= P((X, Y) = (1, 4)) + P((X, Y) = (2, 2)) + P((X, Y) = (2, 4)) \\\\\n&= f(1, 4) + f(2, 2) + f(2, 4) \\\\\n&= 0.05 + 0.25 + 0.15 \\\\\n&= 0.45\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b02a29bd-84e6-51cf-9060-b133a71bcff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158815} {:answer/id #uuid "4b91451b-fd11-5a80-b1dc-fa7c04bcb3d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158816} {:answer/id #uuid "72fa0eee-5a18-5de8-b2fe-ff414da1b07b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158817} {:answer/id #uuid "778c8e40-3034-571f-9228-225abf35f1b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158818} {:answer/id #uuid "7f88975c-fba9-5e5c-bc10-1b1a2